asn.bin, Watch's table from IP address to network and organisation (ADR 0036), is converted from
the IP to ASN Lite database by DB-IP (https://db-ip.com), which DB-IP licenses under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
IP Geolocation by DB-IP: https://db-ip.com

Changes made by the Datapavan project (update.py): ranges of private, reserved and documentation
addresses and AS numbers are dropped, neighbouring ranges of the same AS number are merged, each AS
number keeps one organisation name (the one covering the most addresses, cut at 120 characters),
and the result is written in a binary format of its own. The table is offered under the same
licence; nothing in it is endorsed by DB-IP.

update.py is part of Datapavan's code, under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE at the repository's root).
